.TH CTERMFLUID 1 "November 2026" "CTermFluid" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ctermfluid \- configurable ASCII fluid simulation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctermfluid
.RB [ \-cfmnthV ]
.RB [ \-p " NAME|FILE" ]
.RB [ \-F " FPS" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
CTermFluid animates smoke in a terminal using ncurses.
It runs at a target of 40 simulation updates per second.
The default program creates two opposing plumes.
Press q, Escape, or Ctrl+C to quit. Resizing resets the simulation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-no-color ", " \-\-no-colour
Disable colors. Color is enabled by default on 256-color terminals, with
monochrome fallback when unavailable. The long options \-\-color and
\-\-colour explicitly enable color again.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fps
Show frame rate and simulation statistics.
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-max-fps " N"
Cap rendering at N frames per second (integer 1 to 240, default 40).
Overrides max_fps in the program file; simulation updates remain at 40 Hz.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mouse
Start empty. Drag the left mouse button to add smoke and velocity.
The terminal must support xterm-compatible mouse reporting.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-program " NAME|FILE"
Select a named program or an explicit .conf file. Default: default.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no-dissipation
Disable dye dissipation, overriding the program's setting.
Smoke can eventually saturate the screen.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-check-config
Validate the selected program and exit without starting ncurses.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Programs use INI-style .conf files. A [simulation] section accepts max_fps
(integer 1 to 240, default 40) and dissipation
(0 to 10, default 0.05), viscosity (0 to 1, default 0.0001), and mouse_color
(#RRGGBB, default #00ffff).
The optional mouse_palette key (integer 0 to 15) overrides mouse_color from
the terminal palette in color mouse mode; a failed query keeps mouse_color.
.PP
Each repeated [source] section requires x and y (0 to 1, left/top to
right/bottom), and color (#RRGGBB). Optional keys are radius (integer 0 to 20,
default 3), vx and vy (-1000 to 1000, default 0), rate (0 to 100, default 3),
and palette (integer 0 to 15). Positive velocities point right/down.
Palette is an optional terminal palette override used in color mode;
unsupported queries retain the configured RGB color.
Configured palette colors are refreshed asynchronously about once per second.
New smoke follows theme changes; existing smoke retains its color.
.PP
There can be at most 32 sources. Mouse mode ignores emitters but retains the
simulation settings. Dissipation of zero disables fading. Semicolons introduce
comments; full lines starting with # are also comments.
.PP
Unknown sections or keys, duplicate keys, and invalid values are errors.
.SH FILES
Named programs are searched under $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ctermfluid
(or $HOME/.config/ctermfluid), then ./programs for source-directory use.
Only absolute XDG_CONFIG_HOME paths are used.
Run sudo make install to install the executable in /usr/bin (default prefix /usr),
its manual, and its license. Run CTermFluid without sudo. Missing bundled
programs are created in the running user's config directory on first use.
Installation does not create root-owned user configuration files.
Existing configurations are not overwritten and uninstall preserves them.
An argument containing a slash or ending in .conf is opened directly.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ctermfluid
ctermfluid -p crossflow
ctermfluid -mn
ctermfluid -t -p ./custom.conf
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on a successful check, help/version request, or clean exit;
nonzero on invalid arguments, invalid configuration, or terminal startup failure.
.SH LIMITS
The maximum visible simulation area is 1024 columns by 512 rows.
Extra terminal space is left blank. Native Windows is not supported.
